Title:
test(mocks): add manual jest mocks and unit tests for UserPerson container

Description:
This PR adds reusable manual Jest mocks and focused unit tests for the UserPerson container to improve test reliability and maintainability.

Changes included:
- Add manual mock for userRepository
  - Path: src/features/user/repositories/__mocks__/userRepository.ts
  - Exports: mockUser, ensureTemplateUser, updateUser, createUser
- Add manual mock for useDebouncedSave hook
  - Path: src/features/user/hooks/__mocks__/useDebouncedSave.ts
  - Exports: useDebouncedSave returning debouncedSave, flush, cancel
- Add snapshot test for UserPersonContainer
  - Path: src/features/user/screens/UserPerson/__tests__/UserPerson.container.snapshot.test.tsx
  - Uses manual mocks and a minimal screen mock to focus snapshot on container behavior
- Add autosave behavior unit test for UserPersonContainer
  - Path: src/features/user/screens/UserPerson/__tests__/UserPerson.container.autosave.test.tsx
  - Verifies debouncedSave is called on field change and flush/cancel are called on unmount
- Minor fixes to tests to comply with Jest mock factory restrictions (mock variables prefixed with `mock`)

Why:
- Centralized manual mocks reduce duplication and avoid inline factory pitfalls.
- Tests are deterministic and independent of external services.
- Improves maintainability and makes future test additions simpler.

How to review:
1. Run the test suite locally: `yarn jest --runInBand`
2. Inspect the new `__mocks__` modules for expected exported behavior.
3. Review the two new tests for clarity and coverage of container behavior.

Checklist:
- [x] Tests pass locally
- [x] Manual mocks added next to production modules
- [x] Snapshot added and verified
- [x] Autosave behavior test added and verified

Notes:
- No production code was changed.
- If you prefer the repository mocks to live in a centralized test utilities folder instead of adjacent `__mocks__` folders, we can refactor in a follow-up PR.
